Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Loading a Subpackage", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998592565152832*^9, 3.998592568836899*^9}},
 CellID->1614187768,ExpressionUUID->"acfa7cbb-254d-4455-96e5-26f9e5238cbc"],

Cell["\<\
By default, the master loader initializes only the stable 1D wavepacket \
engine. However, the introspection framework dynamically adapts whenever a \
new mathematical engine is loaded into the kernel.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998491182266306*^9, 3.998491242298786*^9}, 
   3.998491521915882*^9, 3.998568738136557*^9, {3.998574051146677*^9, 
   3.99857409487392*^9}, {3.9985741310807533`*^9, 3.998574141753746*^9}, 
   3.998574849254136*^9, {3.99858270289323*^9, 3.998582724335042*^9}, 
   3.998591749539137*^9, 3.998592579863221*^9, 3.998600824381805*^9, {
   3.998601004602935*^9, 3.998601006610701*^9}},
 CellID->20408445,ExpressionUUID->"3adb6e49-4931-45c9-8e6f-3529e290daaa"],

Cell["\<\
To illustrate this extensible architecture, the Classical Trajectory (CT) \
engine subpackage is introduced below. This specific module serves as the \
primary pedagogical example throughout the remainder of this technical note. \
It will be used to illustrate how the central registry's databases manage \
disparate properties, how the namespace bridge prevents symbol shadowing, and \
ultimately, its exact backend codebase is deconstructed piece-by-piece in the \
Math Engines section.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998592621572639*^9, 3.998592626288624*^9}, {
   3.998600470572317*^9, 3.998600475024212*^9}, 3.998600834019534*^9},
 CellID->604199513,ExpressionUUID->"e466c04d-15ab-4b26-ac3a-250c120d948b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load the CT engine subpackage and query the available types.", \
"MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998470725377934*^9, {3.998491251078803*^9, 3.998491261584784*^9}, 
   3.998491532811735*^9, 3.9985687490476227`*^9, 3.998574859520396*^9, {
   3.998582744254158*^9, 3.998582746249502*^9}, 3.99859176971568*^9, {
   3.9985926418659163`*^9, 3.998592650368423*^9}},
 CellID->1264895388,ExpressionUUID->"fe479130-d91b-4281-9e84-c6b46802b254"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<GWPTools`GWPEngineCT`\>\"", "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"GWP", "[", "\"\<Types\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9984912703637342`*^9, 3.998491290092928*^9}, {
  3.99856858799962*^9, 3.9985685888937263`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[20]:=",
 CellID->548727582,ExpressionUUID->"09bc2c56-4cd8-4a11-8a92-d4793ea317d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"1D\"\>", ",", "\<\"CT\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998603467157364*^9, 3.998608584577104*^9, 
  3.998609260464962*^9, 3.9986115475963497`*^9, 3.998612203996957*^9, 
  3.998641404241589*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[21]=",
 CellID->1329889307,ExpressionUUID->"bf6d81ba-c434-4436-9bc9-75c590f83f8d"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Because the 1D and CT engines govern completely different physical paradigms\
\[LongDash]a distributed quantum wavepacket versus a discrete classical point \
particle\[LongDash]they register unique property classes and external \
environments. The framework enables explicit filtering by engine type to \
isolate these capabilities.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998491548980443*^9, 3.998568770208632*^9, 3.9985748786416197`*^9, {
   3.9985815611178427`*^9, 3.998581569235589*^9}, 3.998591809603598*^9, {
   3.99859267923869*^9, 3.9985927059337387`*^9}, 3.9985927462699223`*^9, {
   3.998600506218643*^9, 3.998600524824584*^9}, 3.998600856959045*^9},
 CellID->1059968039,ExpressionUUID->"e263ef0a-57b4-4eb3-88e9-e6ea369887e8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Query the property classes and potential names registered to the 1D engine.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9984915863145647`*^9, 3.998568779280552*^9, 3.9985748884161158`*^9, 
   3.9985918297499037`*^9, {3.9986005571878242`*^9, 3.998600559710483*^9}},
