Cell["\<\
How does the framework seamlessly absorb this new engine without any \
hardcoded frontend updates? Furthermore, how does the dispatcher know that \
the string alias \"Harmonic\" means something entirely different for a 1D \
object versus a CT object? That is the job of the Central Registry.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998491639167595*^9, 3.998491643683959*^9}, 
   3.998568805056437*^9, {3.998574935661645*^9, 3.998574937904469*^9}, {
   3.9985927927516108`*^9, 3.998592796889802*^9}, 3.998600898975876*^9},
 CellID->428483867,ExpressionUUID->"3aff9ec5-e2b2-4ce4-bfa5-6cccf8e8961b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Central Registry", "Section",
 CellID->143603907,ExpressionUUID->"9ccbc0ae-eb70-4460-997a-c70b32970578"],

Cell["\<\
The dynamic introspection capabilities of GWP and GWPObject are entirely \
powered by GWPRegistry.wl. This package acts as the central nervous system \
for the framework, maintaining the global databases that the dispatcher \
relies on to route evaluations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998477637889347*^9, 3.998574962911528*^9},
 CellID->1926729368,ExpressionUUID->"0cc25888-32d2-4b16-b782-8a65e0d913ff"],

Cell["\<\
When the registry is initialized, it establishes a specific set of data \
structures and registration functions. Because these symbols are protected, \
they reside in the GWPTools`GWPRegistry` context. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9984791517999277`*^9, 3.998479165265135*^9}, {
   3.998479813007213*^9, 3.998479813563788*^9}, {3.9985689300967627`*^9, 
   3.9985689485564623`*^9}, {3.9985749712343397`*^9, 3.9985749763009367`*^9}, 
   3.9985833262768087`*^9},
 CellID->710882237,ExpressionUUID->"7fb585d2-809f-43fe-b57c-84daaaaeb361"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {"$GWPRegistry", Cell["\<\
A flat list storing the raw registration chunks for all active physical \
properties.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0ef1824c-73f7-4304-b271-3abfea1d5059"]},
   {"$GWPInformation", Cell["\<\
A nested Association mapping each engine type and property to its structural \
metadata, such as its ShortKey and Signature Classes.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"258a8ab3-3f07-40c0-8314-120f51f4cfea"]},
   {"$GWPPotentials", Cell["\<\
A nested Association mapping each engine type to its registered potential \
models, including their backend developer symbols, user-facing templates, and \
categories.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f3fdfea1-5ddb-4477-a265-8589c6699b6b"]}
  }]], "DefinitionBox",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998583080797534*^9, 3.998583080797612*^9}, {
  3.998583143936623*^9, 3.9985831881313257`*^9}, {3.998583228667532*^9, 
  3.998583237770816*^9}, {3.998601151234239*^9, 3.998601155427503*^9}},
 CellID->2138174340,ExpressionUUID->"6ba22b2e-1555-4b58-9da3-54209b721a66"],

Cell["GWPRegistry database structures.", "Caption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986012967502604`*^9, 3.9986013077050133`*^9}},
 CellID->1380803939,ExpressionUUID->"e3b85b76-ee70-4634-8df6-7a57f86a9699"],

Cell["\<\
As mathematical engines and extensions are loaded, they inject their specific \
capabilities into these global variables using two primary registration \
functions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998479297828393*^9, 3.998479299761278*^9}, 
   3.998575004878867*^9},
 CellID->296755737,ExpressionUUID->"470e5e2e-1b70-4567-ae77-5c2155af6c20"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {"GWPRegisterExtension", Cell["\<\
Parses a formatted list of physical properties (a registry chunk) and injects \
them into $GWPRegistry and $GWPInformation.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1152fed7-cefe-4bc8-acc6-eb6e8941d76d"]},
   {"GWPRegisterPotentials", Cell["\<\
Parses a formatted list of potential models (a potential chunk) and injects \
them into the unified $GWPPotentials database for the specified engine type.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"cbab3f5e-d159-476b-8106-cdf9c9c9753a"]}
  }]], "DefinitionBox",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998583370542358*^9, 3.998583479756194*^9}, {
  3.998601161988872*^9, 3.998601164273039*^9}},
 CellID->2024629303,ExpressionUUID->"e0a908db-8e8f-4481-81fe-00652cce4711"],

Cell["\<\
GWPRegistry functions for adding property and potential data chunks.\
\>", "Caption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986012592317038`*^9, 3.998601272781089*^9}, {
  3.99860131741501*^9, 3.998601328942936*^9}},
 CellID->871579740,ExpressionUUID->"e4bbced0-ac2a-497d-82c8-d751d2584738"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Property Registration Metadata", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998477663851946*^9, 3.998477667069996*^9}, {
  3.998588040321104*^9, 3.998588045337283*^9}},
 CellID->634574863,ExpressionUUID->"bfa47de3-a99b-4a04-92a4-2322b3361dc6"],

Cell["\<\
When an engine registers physical observables, it submits a flat list of \
sublists. Each sublist strictly contains six string elements in the following \
order: {LongName, ShortKey, DynamicClass, StaticClass, Class, EngineType}.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998477686339875*^9, 3.9984776924963903`*^9}, {
   3.99850967572902*^9, 3.998509679504685*^9}, 3.9985750261198997`*^9, {
   3.998583507677227*^9, 3.998583563337171*^9}, {3.998588071280013*^9, 
   3.9985880759704533`*^9}},
 CellID->895931439,ExpressionUUID->"06a9afaa-9d32-40a1-93ca-0ca78acfdc4d"],

Cell["\<\
Supplying both a DynamicClass and a StaticClass is the cornerstone of the \
framework's routing logic. It allows the dispatcher to gracefully route a \
query to a time-independent mathematical signature if an object is \
constructed without an active potential.\
\>", "Text",
