    DynamicModuleValues:>{},
    Initialization:>(TypeSystem`NestedGrid`PackagePrivate`$outputID$$ = 
     CreateUUID[]),
    UnsavedVariables:>{TypeSystem`NestedGrid`PackagePrivate`$outputID$$}],
   Deploy,
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Deploy"],
  Dataset`InterpretDataset[1],
  Editable->False,
  SelectWithContents->True,
  Selectable->False]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998608659531404*^9, 3.998608710941166*^9, 
  3.99860927415018*^9, 3.9986122046958437`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[27]=",
 CellID->2069944216,ExpressionUUID->"c36d5768-2754-4751-92c7-7cc46c073b91"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
If a future extension introduces a fundamentally new mathematical structure, \
the dispatcher must be extended. This requires exactly two modifications \
inside GWPDispatcher.wl: appending the new class record to the hardcoded \
signature taxonomy, and defining a new GWPPropertyDispatch downvalue that \
explicitly pattern-matches the new class string to construct the necessary \
pure Function shell.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998608852970529*^9, 3.998610123978128*^9},
 CellID->53836824,ExpressionUUID->"ec94aa54-2b06-40dc-8450-81836c5917d8"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Developer Namespace Bridge", "Section",
 CellID->1432375756,ExpressionUUID->"3b718f08-fbc8-437a-8766-e8ec2f19e52d"],

Cell["\<\
A primary challenge in modular package development is symbol shadowing across \
different contexts. GWPDeveloper.wl solves this by acting as the master \
namespace bridge. It hoists foundational symbols (such as RA, RX, RP, and \
NORM) into a universally shared developer context. Because every math engine \
and extension loads this package, they all share a unified physics vocabulary.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998517327767272*^9, {3.9985498592959127`*^9, 3.998549866148754*^9}, 
   3.9985756574662113`*^9},
 CellID->647648222,ExpressionUUID->"c2f510f3-b208-4bd4-9d04-5e16641bf400"],

Cell["\<\
This shared dictionary completely eliminates the need for context-prefixing, \
allowing orchestrators like the Superposition engine to natively read and \
evaluate states generated by disparate packages. Furthermore, \
GWPDispatcher.wl heavily relies on this centralized context to securely route \
queries without needing to know the private context of the engine that \
originally generated the math.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998575665380748*^9, 3.9986103765574703`*^9},
 CellID->1576544158,ExpressionUUID->"0a505969-e1e2-48b5-b511-7dcfed175759"],

Cell["\<\
Crucially, when exploring or debugging the backend in a notebook, the \
GWPDeveloper package must be loaded using Get (<<) rather than Needs to \
forcibly push the hidden context onto the active $ContextPath.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->701886200,ExpressionUUID->"2beec887-9c13-45be-a4eb-fc380f1d12f0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Force-load the developer package and inspect the universal parameters. \
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998517933143499*^9, 3.99851793541715*^9}, 
   3.998575724564363*^9, 3.998610393665535*^9},
 CellID->1324426820,ExpressionUUID->"e2e8cf3d-d31b-4fb3-ab79-80edc44a49fc"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"<<", 
  " ", "\"\<GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\>\""}], "\n", "$ContextPath"}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998517967000331*^9, 3.998517971178884*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[28]:=",
 CellID->973562585,ExpressionUUID->"a1629be2-5d04-4b6c-afe3-9ec0faedb703"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"GWPTools`GWPEngineCT`\"\>", ",", "\<\"GWPTools`\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"WFRCrosslinks`\"\>", ",", "\<\"System`\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Global`\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9985817136445007`*^9, 3.998611556788803*^9, 
  3.998612204774778*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[29]=",
 CellID->317356912,ExpressionUUID->"33bdddbb-3d2c-4964-b24b-1a73868f9bb4"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
To maintain a clean architecture, developers must follow a strict protocol \
regarding the location of variable definitions. Universal symbols, such as \
global physical constants and shared state variables, must be defined \
strictly in GWPDeveloper.wl to guarantee that individual engines do not \
overwrite each other's usage statements. Engine-specific macros and \
mathematical function heads are defined at the very top of their respective \
engine files by temporarily opening the GWPDeveloper context.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99852082546307*^9, 3.998520826914806*^9}, {
   3.998520865910431*^9, 3.998520868237186*^9}, 3.998575743792041*^9, {
   3.998610470013713*^9, 3.998610482006569*^9}, {3.998610547186252*^9, 
   3.99861055337866*^9}},
 CellID->1901161303,ExpressionUUID->"22f3fe70-dfad-4eb8-ac12-7830fea2b38e"],

Cell["\<\
Beyond acting as a shared dictionary, the developer package provides internal \
utilities to assist in package extension. GWPUsageTable parses raw \
Mathematica usage strings and formats them into a clean Grid for immediate \
documentation. GWP1DScalarQ is a specialized pattern-matching utility that \
verifies an expression is a scalar symbol or number, preventing unintended \
list-threading.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9985501552885723`*^9, 3.99855015947183*^9}, 
   3.998575945650745*^9, 3.998610332721957*^9},
 CellID->1506817415,ExpressionUUID->"1cbcfc9b-c0df-49be-8c9d-e0571dec3f0e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Use GWPUsageTable to generate a formatted usage table for some of the \
universal variables.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998550209656618*^9, 3.998550240294533*^9}, 
   3.998575959920041*^9},
 CellID->747414099,ExpressionUUID->"4a021f83-15ba-4f27-9f59-66b800fb9f15"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"GWPUsageTable", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"NORM", ",", " ", "MASS", ",", " ", "HBAR"}], "}"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
